{"availability":"available","full":"chelsper/shindig","name":"shindig","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-19T13:36:17Z","updated":"2026-10-09T22:00:26Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://shindig-liart.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://shindig-liart.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:42.755Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:42.755Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:42.755Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T22:06:42.755Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Before deploying this feature, apply db/migrations/022bringsomething.sql to the same Neon database used by DATABASEURL. It adds potluckitems, potluckclaims, transactional write functions and support for the existing potluck feature flag. It preserves existing data, is reapplicable, and does not create items or enable the module for any event. No new environment variables, dependencies, email service or guest accounts are needed.","For an editable event, enable Bring something in RSVP & Hub, save, then review and publish. Under Responses → Bring something, add an item, a short note and the number needed. Hosts can edit, close/reopen items and release a signup with confirmation. These item/claim changes take effect immediately for an enabled published event; they are not private event-draft changes. Closing keeps existing claims and permits guests to cancel. There is no destructive item deletion. The original hard-coded Jasper event remains unchanged.","The public Hub exposes only item descriptions and aggregate availability. Guest names are host-only. Each guest receives a 256-bit private bearer link to change quantity/name or cancel that individual signup; only its purpose-separated SHA-256 hash is stored. The link does not change an RSVP, and no email/text is sent. Guests must save their link; anyone with it can manage that signup. Canceled links remain usable to sign up again. Disabling the module or unpublishing/archiving the event blocks guest access entirely."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/chelsper/shindig/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"78facb1e42a9f5b16b16342668fa33130810fcd27ab2bc176fc5b4c9030c38ee","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:42.864Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:42.864Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Before deploying this feature, apply db/migrations/022bringsomething.sql to the same Neon database used by DATABASEURL. It adds potluckitems, potluckclaims, transactional write functions and support for the existing potluck feature flag. It preserves existing data, is reapplicable, and does not create items or enable the module for any event. No new environment variables, dependencies, email service or guest accounts are needed.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/chelsper/shindig/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"not_required","text":"It is independent of the host-accounts migration 020; 020 is not required just for location setup.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/chelsper/shindig/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Host sign-in returns to that choice; no arbitrary return URL is accepted.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/chelsper/shindig/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"exact authorized redirect URI: This server-redirect flow does not require a browser JavaScript client or Google API keys.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/chelsper/shindig/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"Commercial Shindig use requires the appropriate paid license; the current plans require Professional or higher for historical data.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/chelsper/shindig/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"78facb1e42a9f5b16b16342668fa33130810fcd27ab2bc176fc5b4c9030c38ee","sou